  food_tithe.the_third_year({ask:ezras_penalty})                         ("Ezra's penalty (14:29) — the first tithe's recipient disputed (Yevamot 86a:1, 86a:14), Ezra's penalty on the Levites who did not come up (86b:4-7; KO.the_tithe by CALL): the priest who takes the first tithe after Ezra accepted", ['accepted'])
  food_tithe.the_third_year({ask:one_tithe_not_two})                     ("one tithe not two (14:28) — the poor man's tithe replaces the second in the third and the sixth year (the Sifrei 109:5, 109:10-11; Rosh Hashanah 12b:1-5), the Levite never interrupted (KO.the_tithe by CALL): THE WRITE poor_tithe_owed — a STATUS on Israel at the chapter's own day; the readback row 
  food_tithe.the_third_year({ask:the_animal_tithe_now})                  ("the animal tithe now (14:23) — decreed away in the present (Bekhorot 53b:5); the tenth an ordinal (Mishnah Bekhorot 9:7 — TM.tithe by CALL), the naming's error (YO.tithe_naming): the herdsman today exempt", ['exempt'])
  food_tithe.the_third_year({ask:the_convert_at_the_gate})               ("the convert at the gate (14:29) — 14:29's sojourner the convert (Onkelos; the Sifrei 110:2), a son of the covenant among the four in want (Yevamot 47b; ST, HO by CALL): the convert at the gate accepted", ['accepted'])
  food_tithe.the_third_year({ask:the_courtyard_from_your_gates})         ("the courtyard from 'your gates' (14:29) — the liability by the house (R. Yannai) or the courtyard (R. Yochanan, from 'in your gates') — Bava Metzia 88a:1-2; KO.the_tithe 'thresholds' by CALL: the one whose produce entered the courtyard through its gate accepted as liable", ['accepted'])
  food_tithe.the_third_year({ask:the_four_in_want})                      ('the four in want (14:29) — the Levite, the sojourner, the fatherless and the widow shall come and eat and be satisfied (the Sifrei 110:1-2 — I3; ST by CALL, stranger_love_commanded Deut 10:17 by kind): the widow at the gate accepted', ['accepted'])
  food_tithe.the_third_year({ask:the_gifts_exempt})                      ('the gifts exempt (14:28-29) — the corner, the gleanings and the forgotten sheaf owe no tithe (the Sifrei 109:12; HO.gifts by CALL — the window until the smoothing; the import table names 14:28): the owner who leaves the corner and does not tithe it — left for the poor', ['left_for_the_poor'])
  food_tithe.the_third_year({ask:the_levite_never_interrupted})          ("the Levite never interrupted (14:29) — the first tithe every year, the third too (Rosh Hashanah 12b:4 — R. Yehuda from 'and the Levite shall come', R. Eliezer ben Yaakov from the inheritance): the Levite in the third year accepted", ['accepted'])
  food_tithe.the_third_year({ask:the_measures})                          ("the measures (14:29) — not less than half a kav of wheat, a kav of barley at the threshing floor (Mishnah Peah 8:5-6; Tosefta Peah 4:2, 4:8-10 — 'sufficient for his lack'; HO.gifts by CALL who is poor): the poor man given half a kav of wheat accepted", ['accepted'])
  food_tithe.the_third_year({ask:the_removal_date})                      ("the removal's date (14:28) — the eve of the last festival day of Passover of the fourth and the seventh year (Mishnah Maaser Sheni 5:6; the Sifrei 109:1-3 — I2 with 31:10): THE PARAMETER the_removal_date, the date the calendar's own key; the one who removes the tithes on that eve accepted", ['acce
  food_tithe.the_third_year({ask:the_resident_alien_at_the_gate})        ("the resident alien at the gate (14:21, 14:29) — 14:21's person, sustained with the carcass, not among the four in want (SA.carcass 'who', HO.gifts 'recipients' by CALL): the resident alien at the gate exempt from the poor man's tithe", ['exempt'])
  food_tithe.the_third_year({ask:the_seventh_year_by_the_cycle})         ("the seventh year by the cycle (14:28) — the third and the sixth work years, the seventh the sabbath of the land (YO.cycle by CALL; CA.sabbatical 'land released in year 7'; the Sifrei 109:4): the one who would tithe the seventh year's produce exempt", ['exempt'])
  food_tithe.the_third_year({ask:the_tithes_new_year})                   ("the tithes' new year (14:28) — Tishri 1 with the first third beside it, the tree's the fifteenth of Shevat (Rosh Hashanah 12a:6-9, 12b:9-11, 13a:3; Mishnah Rosh Hashanah 1:1): THE PARAMETER the_tithes_new_year; the one who tithes by the first third accepted", ['accepted'])
  food_tithe.the_third_year({ask:the_uses_barred})                       ("the uses barred (14:29) — no debt, no ransom, no wedding gift, no charity from the poor man's tithe (Tosefta Peah 4:16); its non-separation makes untithed produce (Yevamot 86a:4): the poor man who pays a debt from it barred from it", ['barred_from_it'])
